1
00:00:00,850 --> 00:00:04,736
Once a year, the preserver of the world goes to sleep.

2
00:00:05,050 --> 00:00:15,630
On a night in the rainy season, Devshayani Ekadashi, Vishnu lies down on the serpent Shesha, on the cosmic ocean, and closes his eyes.

3
00:00:16,250 --> 00:00:21,718
For four months, the monsoon months, he sleeps. This time is called Chaturmas.

4
00:00:31,150 --> 00:00:33,350
The rain comes.

5
00:00:37,150 --> 00:00:39,350
The rivers rise.

6
00:00:43,150 --> 00:00:46,028
The fields turn green, then gold.

7
00:00:49,750 --> 00:00:51,986
And the lamps of autumn are lit.

8
00:00:57,450 --> 00:01:03,222
Then, on Prabodhini Ekadashi, the day of awakening, he opens his eyes.

9
00:01:03,650 --> 00:01:11,648
Homes celebrate by marrying a sacred basil plant, Tulsi, to Vishnu, under a canopy of sugarcane.

10
00:01:12,050 --> 00:01:14,898
And the season of weddings begins again.

11
00:01:18,850 --> 00:01:24,716
Even asleep, he holds the world. And every year, the world waits for him to wake.
